     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Ale, <div><br></div><div>Thanks for including data, but your example made me do a little too much work to get to the answer :/ </div><div><br></div><div>my_map &lt;- qmap(&quot;nigeria&quot;, zoom = 6, color = &quot;bw&quot;, legend = &quot;topleft&quot;)<br></div><div><div><br></div><div>my_map +</div></div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><div>stat_density2d( aes( x = coords.x1,  y = coords.x2, fill = ..level.., alpha = ..level..),  geom = &quot;polygon&quot;, mydata) +</div></div><div><div>scale_alpha(guide=FALSE) ## this is the part you probably need</div></div></blockquote><br><div><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2/attach/bbc55da5cc35c/NigeriaOverlay.png?part=0.1&amp;view=1\" alt=\"Inline image 1\" width=\"409\" height=\"409\"><br></div><div><br></div><div>That gets rid of the alpha legend. </div><div><br></div><div>B</div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
